 ### [Voxel and Grid-Based Prediction](15382-voxel-and-grid-based-prediction.md)
+This family of methods predicts 3D Gaussian Splatting parameters by conditioning on a discrete voxel or grid representation, rather than generating them directly from continuous features or pixel-aligned projections. It solves the problem of spatial coherence and efficient memory usage in feed-forward reconstruction by localizing predictions to grid cells. It differs from its siblings by explicitly using a voxel grid as the primary latent structure for attribute prediction, contrasting with Textured-GS which uses triplanes, and 3D Skew-Normal Splatting which focuses on distributional properties rather than grid alignment.
 
 ### GSGEN
